ing), <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars-owned (company fleet)</b> (no owner; all of its revenue is CarmaCars&#39;) or <b class="gd-ui">A partner rental company&#39;s car</b> (choose the partner; leave the commission empty to use the partner&#39;s).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The daily rate is filled in from similar cars, else the class. Keep it, change it, or empty it and set the rates later on the car&#39;s Rates tab. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The title, description and features are written by themselves right after the car is added, from the VIN details. Change any of them on the car&#39;s listing; a field you change is kept.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every car gets a fleet number and its standard settings the moment it is added: a complete rate card (the daily rate you typed or the suggested one, weekend, weekly and monthly from it, the kilometres a day, the extra kilometre rate, the deposit and the delivery and pickup fee of its class) and drivers 18 to 20 allowed. Each value set this way says (Set automatically) on the car&#39;s Overview and Rates tab until you change it. The defaults come from Settings: Program and Fee defaults.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A VIN that does not add up (one character misread) shows a warning; you can still save it. A VIN the decoder cannot read asks only the year, make and model and never stops you: the details fill in when it is read later. The duplicate check runs as for every car: a VIN only once, a plate on one active car, and a likely twin waits for you in Similar cars before it is published.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The gearbox comes from the government&#39;s fuel economy data for the model when it has one gearbox for it, or from the VIN when the VIN states it. Seats come from the VIN, else from the seat table for 3-row SUVs and minivans (a Yukon XL or a Palisade is 8, 7 with captain&#39;s chairs), else 4 for a coupe or convertible and 5 for a sedan or hatchback. An SUV or minivan with neither is left without seats and shows Seats missing in Vehicles: the 7+ seats filter cannot show it until you set them. When either is not certain, Admin &gt; Today shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirm gearbox and seats</b>: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows <b class="gd-ui">Pick the trim</b> there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.</p><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b> shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-partners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a partner</b>: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Banking (Admins only): <b class="gd-ui">Save the payout account</b> for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b> once checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Portal: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to the owner portal</b> gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The partner signs only in the portal, with the e-signature: a signature on paper is not recorded. <b class="gd-ui">Read the partner agreement</b> shows the text they sign.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-fleet-on-its-own-rates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner fleet on its own rates</h2><p class="gd-p">Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> &gt; the partner. <b class="gd-ui">Pricing</b> shows how it works: our base rate is the partner&#39;s listed rate less the partner discount (10% unless you set another), to the nearest dollar; then every rule of our own cars applies (the weekend rate, lead-time pricing, promo codes, the non-refundable discount), with every fee, the deposit and HST. CarmaCars receives a kickback of 20% of the listed rental (the partner&#39;s rates times the days booked); the partner is owed the rest. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit pricing</b> to change the discount, the kickback or the basis for every car at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> lists each car with its listed rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and our base rates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own discount or kickback, mark it <b class="gd-ui">Insurance included</b> or <b class="gd-ui">No credit card needed</b>, or confirm its model year. Our rates change at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Kickback and payable</b> lists each rental: the listed rental, the kickback receivable, the amount payable to the partner and our rental charge, with the totals not on a statement yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and &quot;Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review&quot;. A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says &quot;Year confirmed when you book&quot;; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car&#39;s page before its first handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), <b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">3 days on the C43 AMG Blue, booked 3 weeks ahead</th><th scope="col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Listed rental (3 x $225)</td><td>$675.00</td></tr><tr><td>Our rental charge (3 x $203, the listed rate less 10%)</td><td>$609.00</td></tr><tr><td>Booked ahead −5%</td><td>−$30.45</td></tr><tr><td>Fees (delivery, young driver and the like) and HST</td><td>CarmaCars&#39; own, 100%</td></tr><tr><td>Kickback receivable (20% of $675)</td><td>$135.00</td></tr><tr><td>Payable to the partner</td><td>$540.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The partner&#39;s monthly statement shows each rental at the listed rate, the kickback and the amount payable; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner&#39;s share in proportion; our discount, lead-time pricing and any discount CarmaCars gives do not. Offers sent and bookings confirmed before the change keep their prices and are paid as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-s-crm-01-motors-gohighlevel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner&#39;s CRM (01 Motors&#39; GoHighLevel)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> tile, then the partner (or <b class="gd-ui">CRM link</b> on the partner&#39;s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box <b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors gives us</b> on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press <b class="gd-ui">Connect</b>. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. <b class="gd-ui">Test connection</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Run sync now</b> do it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors sees</b>: CarmaCars&#39; own cars and program owners&#39; cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a &quot;CarmaCars Vehicles&quot; object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner&#39;s. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change what we share</b> to leave out program owners&#39; cars, rates, availability or photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Partner price</b>: the site&#39;s rates, or the site&#39;s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Their cars coming in</b>: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows <b class="gd-ui">Add as their car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Leads both ways</b> (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Feed, widget and booking links</b>: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/&lt;car&gt; that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin &gt; Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-add-a-rental-by-hand" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental by hand</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> at the top of Bookings (or on To do). For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Standing with the renter at pickup? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: type the renter&#39;s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner using own car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter&#39;s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner&#39;s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b> once the insurer confirms it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer&#39;s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press <b class="gd-ui">Add another payment (paid in parts)</b> and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">15</span><div class="gd-t">The rental agreement is sent to sign online (a rental agreement signed on paper is not accepted). The calendar: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">16</span><div class="gd-t">Tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b> if they should not get the confirmation. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal (never on paper). With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Verified in person</b> records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-retire-or-delete-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Retire or delete a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Retire or delete</b>, or the car&#39;s own page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Retire this car</b> takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> brings it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete this car</b> removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the same page, <b class="gd-ui">Delete all sample cars</b> deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-sample-cars-on-the-site" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample cars on the site</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site</b>. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide sample cars</b> asks first (&quot;Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?&quot;); press <b class="gd-ui">Hide them</b> to take every sample car off the site at once, or <b class="gd-ui">Keep them</b>. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show sample cars</b> puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the site each one is marked &quot;Example car&quot;. They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-why-a-car-is-not-on-the-site-yet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Why a car is not on the site yet</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the card Not on the site yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The same car is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The car comes off both once it is on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-placeholder-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Placeholder bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b> (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a placeholder</b>. Not once money was taken or the car went out. <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking</b> undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Competing for these dates</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Also on this car for these dates</b> once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-tolls-when-two-rentals-overlap" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tolls when two rentals overlap</h2><p class="gd-p">Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-service', 'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets the receipt, not an invoice.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). How the owner signs: by email, or on paper.
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid, the owner gets the receipt and the two prepaid months count. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. Cars and terms, at the top: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
2. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
3. Owner: address, sign-in, agreements, and what is still missing for the registry forms.
4. Statements and payouts for this owner.
5. Forms C and D, with a link to the review queue.
6. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Record signed on paper (with the date) and Withdraw it. One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. In History, **Record signed on paper** or **Withdraw it**.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper, Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Signed on paper? Press **Record paper signature**. Choose the Document, check Signed by and Date signed, add the witnesses where the form needs them, and upload the scan of every signed page.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Record paper signature**. Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. A paper signature counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Form C is signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witness on the same screen. Form D (and Form C on paper, if the owner prefers) is printed, signed in front of witnesses, and sent as a photo of each page.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him, and Forms C and D are not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.
