  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> (payments, deposits, refunds), <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), <b class="gd-ui">All payments</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Refunds</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposits</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b> lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.</p><section class="gd-task" id="finance-your-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg" alt="The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.3%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At the end of the day count the drawer and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>. The difference shows &quot;balanced&quot;, or &quot;over&quot; or &quot;short&quot; with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-deposits-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments, deposits, refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds in progress. Press <b class="gd-ui">Request the refund</b> and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/money</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/865"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="865"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.6%;top:60.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.4%;top:21.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:45.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-payment-received-another-way" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A payment received another way</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoice: on <b class="gd-ui">Payments, deposits, refunds</b>, find it under Owner invoices owing and press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Renter: beside the failed payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>. Or open the booking&#39;s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.</p><p class="gd-p">Each month&#39;s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-cards-holds-and-deposits-given-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cards, holds and deposits given back</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Rental charges, <b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b>: extra kilometres, fuel, damage, a late return on the card on file, with the reason on the renter&#39;s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason (the rest is released), or <b class="gd-ui">Release</b>. While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-settle-a-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle a deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (<b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b>) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-read-a-toll-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a toll notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked against the notice</b> on each line (<b class="gd-ui">Leave out</b> to skip one), then <b class="gd-ui">Save as checked</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Confirm and import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/580"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="580"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.5%;top:44.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:64.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>In the work queue, <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b> retries the match after a fix, and <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b> marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg" alt="The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:12.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-reconciliation-and-turo-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reconciliation and Turo trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> tab: press <b class="gd-ui">Record a processor payout</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turo trips</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Add a trip</b> for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/turo</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.1%;top:14.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposits-to-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits to release</h2><p class="gd-p">A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: &quot;Release the deposit for&quot; the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task: it opens the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="