="gd-ui">Clock out for them</b>, set the time they finished and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-daily-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Daily checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Daily checks</b> and choose <b class="gd-ui">Opening check</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Closing check</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the opening check</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Save the closing check</b>). You can save it again.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/checks</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/820"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:15.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:44.7%;top:42%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:64.2%;top:94%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking press <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b>; on a booking on rent, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Afterwards press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> and a reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-photo-reviews-after-a-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photo reviews after a return</h2><p class="gd-p">After each return, the field photo set waits under <b class="gd-ui">Photo reviews</b>. Compare it with the pickup set. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review done</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a re-shoot</b> if a photo is missing or unclear.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-similar-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Similar cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car&#39;s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs and its <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> and check it; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-in: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">An urgent To do &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot; means the renter pressed <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter&#39;s photos), then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> takes the VIN from the car: <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> in the door frame or under the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>; drag the extras into their order in the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo&#39;s edge is cut off by itself. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b>, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under a photo to make it again without it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-screen-many-photos-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One screen, many photos (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter&#39;s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car&#39;s page, record <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return to owner</b> with photos: the owner sees them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-repair-costs-on-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repair costs on a car</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'sales', 'chapter', 'fleet', 'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Save and send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 24 hours unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.
', 'Sales', 'Requests and offers, new quotes and owner leads.',
  'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Save and send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 24 hours unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.
