The check-out is one screen too: the actual return time (late charges follow it), km, fuel, photos and a note. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.</p><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-take-the-car-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take the car back</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Car and keys received: confirm you have the car and its keys.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Odometer, then Fuel or charge, as at pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Keys and extras: count what came back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cleanliness: inside and out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Photo set: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Compare with pickup: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b> and take a close-up photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Renter reviews and signs. Then you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>. The check-out time is the moment you press it: a late return, the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it automatically. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If the renter already pressed I&#39;ve returned the car, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">The check-out is one screen too: the actual return time (late charges follow it), km, fuel, photos and a note. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'photo-shoots', 'chapter', 'a-return', 'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under **More outside photos** (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under **Other detail** (up to 20).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

The steps at the top say where the listing is: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press **Remove** under that photo, then **Remove it**, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.

**Add photos** takes up to 30 photos at once from the camera roll, in any order: each is sorted to its shot by itself. Take at least 10, the whole car outside from every side, then the inside. A watermark or caption at the edge of a photo is cut off by itself; a photo with one in the middle is kept off the site, so take your own photos rather than saving a dealer''s.', 'Photo shoots', 'Shoot a listing''s photos in order and submit them.',
  'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Photos that fit no shot go in with **Extra outside photos** (any number, placed on the studio background like the others) or **Extra inside and detail photos** (any number).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

The steps at the top say where the listing is: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press **Remove** under that photo, then **Remove it**, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.

**Add photos** takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll, in any order: each is sorted to its shot by itself. Take at least 10, the whole car outside from every side, then the inside. A watermark or caption at the edge of a photo is cut off by itself; a photo with one in the middle is kept off the site, so take your own photos rather than saving a dealer''s.',
  '<p class="gd-p">A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.</p><section class="gd-task" id="photo-shoots-shoot-the-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shoot the listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press <b class="gd-ui">I have read this</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot (or <b class="gd-ui">From photos</b> to pick one you took). <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> to redo one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An upload failed? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Photos that fit no shot go in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (any number, placed on the studio background like the others) or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (any number).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/730"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="730"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:34.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:67.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:97.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The steps at the top say where the listing is: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under that photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Keep other cars&#39; plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car&#39;s plate before the listing goes live.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll, in any order: each is sorted to its shot by itself. Take at least 10, the whole car outside from every side, then the inside. A watermark or caption at the edge of a photo is cut off by itself; a photo with one in the middle is kept off the site, so take your own photos rather than saving a dealer&#39;s.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'report-rentals-referrals-and-profile', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. Open **Report a problem** and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. Open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.

## Alerts

The bell at the top opens **Alerts**: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (**Alerts** > **Settings**), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has **Mark picked up** (it opens the booking) and **Snooze 30 min**. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.', 'Report, rentals, referrals and profile', 'Report an incident, add a rental, commissions, your referral link and your profile.',
  'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

